"""
External Tool Adapters — Safe wrappers for tools outside the kernel boundary.

These are NOT kernel modules. They are developer tools that wrap external
processes (e.g., npx repomix) with safety gates. No external tool is ever
imported as a Python dependency.

Rule: truth_source is ALWAYS False for all external outputs.

Phase 1: Capability Adapter Contract — universal contract for all external
Phase 2: Intelligence Plane Registry — unified registry for all adapters
Phase 3: External Evidence Model — all external outputs are EVIDENCE, never TRUTH
Phase 4: Context Engineering Plane — formalized context-pack planning, inspection, evidence
Phase 5: Memory Intelligence Plane — external memory provider contracts, policies, evidence
Phase 8: Skill Evolution Plane — proposal-only skill evolution, policy, profiles, evidence
Phase 9: Orchestration Policy Layer — dry-run planning, policy profiles, evidence bundles
capabilities (context, memory, agent, ide, eval, skill, usage, tool).
"""

